ETHERNET / LAN

-   CSMA/CD: sense → send → collision → abort → backoff [0, 2^min(n,10)−1]
    slots.
-   64 B minimum = sender still transmitting when worst-case collision
    returns.
-   Switch: learn src MAC→port; forward known unicast; flood
    unknown/broadcast; age out.
-   Switches split collision domains; VLANs split broadcast domains.
-   STP: root bridge (lowest ID) → root ports → block redundant links. Slow;
    RSTP faster.
-   802.1Q: 12-bit VLAN tag; trunk = tagged.
-   Wi-Fi: CSMA/CA (can't detect collisions while sending) + ACK; hidden
    terminal → RTS/CTS.

